# Convolutional layer: numerical example

Step-by-step application of the formulas from [layers/conv2d.md](../layers/conv2d.md) with every complication present at once: an RGB image (three channels), a non-square image, a non-square kernel, padding and a stride larger than one. All values are small integers, so every step can be verified by hand. The numbers below are generated and checked against the actual layer implementation and Gorgonia gradients by [cmd/docsgen](../../cmd/docsgen).

