Channels G and B are padded the same way.

## Output size

$$H' = \left\lfloor \frac{ {{- .Height}} + 2 \cdot {{.PadH}} - {{.KernelH -}} }{ {{- .StrideH -}} } \right\rfloor + 1 = {{.OutH}} \qquad W' = \left\lfloor \frac{ {{- .Width}} + 2 \cdot {{.PadW}} - {{.KernelW -}} }{ {{- .StrideW -}} } \right\rfloor + 1 = {{.OutW}} \tag{ {{- .OutSizeTag -}} }$$

The non-square kernel makes the two directions differ on purpose: the output is ${{.OutH}} \times {{.OutW}}$ per filter.

## Forward

An output element of filter $o$ at position $(i, j)$ is the sum over all three channels of elementwise products between the ${{.KernelH}} \times {{.KernelW}}$ window of $\tilde{x}$ starting at row $i \cdot s_h$, column $j \cdot s_w$ and the kernel slice of the channel.

